WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.819
Imagine Roliat.

00:00:00.819 --> 00:00:08.193
Her family has moved from a village to a town, and she is returning to school after interrupted

00:00:08.193 --> 00:00:08.602
education.

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:10.241
She speaks Yoruba confidently.

00:00:10.241 --> 00:00:12.699
She is still learning to read.

00:00:12.699 --> 00:00:15.566
She has watched vegetables grow at home.

00:00:15.566 --> 00:00:18.843
Now her teacher asks her to explain photosynthesis.

00:00:18.843 --> 00:00:20.892
The textbook is in English.

00:00:20.892 --> 00:00:24.578
Roliat looks down at the page and stays quiet.

00:00:24.578 --> 00:00:25.807
She is curious.

00:00:25.807 --> 00:00:28.675
She needs a way into the lesson.

00:00:28.675 --> 00:00:29.084
òye.

00:00:29.084 --> 00:00:34.000
starts with what she wants to understand, in a language she understands.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.500
This is òye.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:37.500
Learning that understands you.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:43.500
We will start in English so you can follow the learning loop.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.000
A photosynthesis request creates a learning journey.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:53.000
The app asks about your starting point, then opens a sourced lesson.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:01:00.000
The lesson explains the process, gives a visual summary, and keeps the source visible.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.136
Now the important part.

00:01:02.136 --> 00:01:07.476
The learner says that sunlight becomes the material in sugar.

00:01:07.476 --> 00:01:08.010
òye.

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:11.748
asks a follow-up before giving corrective feedback.

00:01:11.748 --> 00:01:19.757
It checks what the learner means, then identifies the misconception using words from the answer.

00:01:19.757 --> 00:01:22.961
The repair separates materials from energy.

00:01:22.961 --> 00:01:26.699
Carbon dioxide and water are materials used.

00:01:26.699 --> 00:01:28.301
Light supplies energy.

00:01:28.301 --> 00:01:30.971
Carbohydrates and oxygen are products.

00:01:30.971 --> 00:01:38.981
A later explanation and a fresh application check whether the learner can use that distinction.

00:01:38.981 --> 00:01:45.388
The new answer correctly treats sunlight as energy, rather than sugar material.

00:01:45.388 --> 00:01:47.524
Both attempts stay saved.

00:01:47.524 --> 00:01:50.728
Progress changes because of the evidence.

00:01:50.728 --> 00:01:55.000
Watching a video alone does not establish understanding.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:57.667
Now let us learn in Yoruba.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.889
A teacher helps Roliat begin.

00:01:59.889 --> 00:02:03.000
She can start by speaking her question.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:12.216
Mo fẹ́ kọ́ nípa photosynthesis. Báwo ni àwọn ohun ọ̀gbìn ṣe ń ṣe oúnjẹ wọn?

00:02:12.216 --> 00:02:12.754
òye.

00:02:12.754 --> 00:02:14.370
recognizes the request.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:19.216
Here it is reading a starting question in Yoruba.

00:02:19.216 --> 00:02:26.900
Kí ni àwọn ohun ọ̀gbìn gbọ́dọ̀ lo láti ṣe oúnjẹ wọn nípasẹ̀ photosynthesis?

00:02:29.216 --> 00:02:34.105
Her course includes explanations, a diagram and sources.

00:02:34.105 --> 00:02:36.549
Here is a video.

00:02:36.549 --> 00:02:40.216
The explanation is in Yoruba too.

00:02:40.216 --> 00:02:44.266
Carbon Dioxide àti Omi Nínú Photosynthesis

00:02:44.266 --> 00:02:52.272
Àwọn ohun ọ̀gbìn ń lo carbon dioxide àti omi papọ̀
láti ṣe carbohydrates àti oxygen.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:59.241
Ìmọ́lẹ̀ oòrùn ń pèsè agbára fún ìṣe yìí. [s1] Àwọn
ohun èlò àti àwọn ọjà

00:02:59.241 --> 00:03:00.216
Nínú photosynthesis, àwọn ohun ọ̀gbìn lo carbon
dioxide àti omi láti ṣe carbohydrates—oúnjẹ—àti
oxygen. [s1]

00:03:00.216 --> 00:03:06.108
Learners can choose English, Yoruba, Hausa and Igbo for their lessons.

00:03:06.108 --> 00:03:12.000
Save text for later, and keep learning when the connection drops.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:15.886
Codex worked through this project from the beginning.

00:03:15.886 --> 00:03:19.286
AGENTS.md records our stack and working rules.

00:03:19.286 --> 00:03:23.171
The plan divides the build into small milestones.

00:03:23.171 --> 00:03:26.086
Decisions document what changed and why.

00:03:26.086 --> 00:03:31.429
During review, we found that clearing history could reset usage limits.

00:03:31.429 --> 00:03:35.314
Codex implemented retained counters and checked them separately.

00:03:35.314 --> 00:03:38.714
The Agents SDK runs the app's AI.

00:03:38.714 --> 00:03:40.171
Codex powered development.

00:03:40.171 --> 00:03:46.000
Setup, architecture and deployment notes give another developer a place to start.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:54.816
With another month, we would pilot with learners and teachers, measure how misconceptions improve, refine translations and deploy

00:03:54.816 --> 00:03:56.286
a hosted pilot.

00:03:56.286 --> 00:03:59.224
For Roliat, the aim is concrete.

00:03:59.224 --> 00:04:00.694
Hear an idea.

00:04:00.694 --> 00:04:02.653
Make sense of it.

00:04:02.653 --> 00:04:05.592
Explain it in her own words.

00:04:05.592 --> 00:04:06.082
òye.

00:04:06.082 --> 00:04:07.061
Learn anything.

00:04:07.061 --> 00:04:08.531
In your language.

00:04:08.531 --> 00:04:10.000
In your way.
